  "Question": "If four times the reciprocal of the circumference of a circle equals the diameter of the circle, then the area of the circle is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac1{\\pi^2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac1\\pi\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\pi\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\pi^2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Let the radius be \\(r>0\\). The circumference is \\(2\\pi r\\), and the diameter is \\(2r\\), so the given condition becomes\n\\[\n\\frac4{2\\pi r}=2r.\n\\]\nMultiplying by the nonzero circumference \\(2\\pi r\\) gives \\(4=4\\pi r^2\\), hence \\(\\pi r^2=1\\). This is already the area formula, so there is no need to find the radius separately. The area is \\(1\\), choice C.",
